  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 138 AM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nTemperatures remain above normal through the end of the week,\nperhaps ticking up a couple of more degrees expanding triple digit\nheat to much of the Permian Basin by Saturday. Models are backing\noff on a cold front that earlier had been depicted as reaching the\nbasin. It now appears the front will stall to the north of the\narea, but the associated upper trough should erode the southern\nplains high enough to allow for slightly cooler temperatures by\nearly next week. The high pressure center shifts from our west\nlate in the week, to the east early next week allowing for cooler\ngulf air to advect into West Texas and eastern New Mexico. \nGreater moisture could also allow for better rain chances next \nweek and the NBM is showing slight chance to low chance (20-40%) \nPoPs. The lack of any upper support prevents rain chances from \ngetting any better. \n\nHennig",
